# Line endings matter here in a way they usually do not.
#
# The shell scripts are run on Android. A CRLF shebang fails with
# "bad interpreter: /data/data/.../bash^M: no such file or directory", which is a confusing
# error for a file that looks correct in an editor - and git's `core.autocrlf` on Windows
# rewrites them on checkout without asking.
#
# `text eol=lf` stores them with LF and checks them out with LF on every platform, so the
# scripts survive a round trip through a Windows working copy. Editing them on Windows needs
# an editor that preserves LF; most do, and git will convert on commit if it does not.
*.sh   text eol=lf

# Python is not picky, but the same rule keeps the tree stable between the two machines.
*.py   text eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.webp binary
*.zip  binary
*.sqlite3 binary

# Installable packages: never line-ending converted.
*.apk  binary
*.keystore binary
